            <ArticleTitle>[Metatarsalgia caused by compression of the internal plantar nerve].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>90-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The Author has presented a rare form of internal plantar nerve compression that was produced by a synovial cystic formation, which caused a plantar pain during the load that radiated to the first three toes. Besides he has considered the other possible causes of metatarsus pain for alterations of soft parts.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
